menu "StampFly Research Features"

    config SF_ENABLE_SNN
        bool "Build the research SNN estimator and controller"
        default n
        help
            Builds the research spiking neural network (SNN, CUBA-LIF) attitude
            estimator and controller (sf_estimator_snn, sf_controller_snn,
            sf_snn_core) into the firmware, so that estimator.type = 2 and
            controller.type = 1 can be selected. The weights are an UNTRAINED
            placeholder (fixed random values); in SILS the vehicle is expected
            to crash (emergency DISARM about 1 s after takeoff).

            Enabling this uses about 31 KB of the internal RAM (a fixed
            variable area, because the SNN objects are static). The chip has
            no external RAM and only about 37 KB is free after boot, so leave
            this disabled for any build that is flown for real.

            When disabled (the default), estimator.type = 2 and
            controller.type = 1 are not available: the firmware logs a warning
            and starts with the default implementation (ESKF / PID).

endmenu
